179
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:19,580
Yeah, you're right.

180
00:11:19,580 --> 00:11:23,960
Wow, this guy isn't even trying.

181
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:27,020
Looks like the only cards he's obtained are for food and water.

182
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:30,600
Actually, that can make it a lot easier to invite them.

183
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:34,300
But if it really is a member of the troop, we won't invite them.

184
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:35,900
We'll see what they say.

185
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:36,900
Yeah?

186
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:38,940
What's the point of even trying?

187
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:41,240
We already know it's one of them.

188
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:43,900
We need to know who they are, but why they're here is more important.

189
00:11:43,900 --> 00:11:45,900
What are you, a damn idiot?

190
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:48,900
Are you just going to ask them why they're here?

191
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:51,900
Because big surprise, they're not going to tell you.

192
00:11:51,900 --> 00:11:55,900
Yeah, I'm an idiot, fine, but I'm still going to ask and you can't stop me.

193
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:56,900
Then go right ahead.

194
00:11:56,900 --> 00:11:57,900
Great.

195
00:11:57,900 --> 00:11:58,900
Maybe I will.

196
00:11:58,900 --> 00:11:59,900
Are they okay?

197
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:01,900
This kind of thing happens every day.

198
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:02,900
I'm going.

199
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:05,900
Then quit yapping and just do it.

200
00:12:05,900 --> 00:12:06,900
Accompany on!

201
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:07,900
Crawl a low silver!

202
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:08,900
Crawl a low silver!

203
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:09,900
Then quit yapping and just do it!

204
00:12:09,900 --> 00:12:10,900
Accompany on!

205
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:12,900
Crawl a low silver!

206
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:29,160
The next part is to make it look always possible so you can watch a time, but it is okay...

207
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:48,400
No way.

208
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:50,300
Hisoka!

209
00:12:50,300 --> 00:12:52,800
Hmm.

210
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:57,200
What have we here?

211
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:59,960
It seems I have unexpected guests.

212
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:01,760
Long time no see.

213
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,820
Just as I suspected.

214
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:14,260
You've matured quite a lot, haven't you?

215
00:13:15,140 --> 00:13:17,660
You've clearly found an excellent teacher.

216
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:23,040
You'll continue to ripen into sweet fruit, just as I thought.

217
00:13:24,560 --> 00:13:27,000
Okay, so do you guys actually know this, pervert?

218
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:30,180
Ah, you must be their teacher, I assume.

219
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:32,760
No, doesn't seem the type.

220
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:35,440
Ah! Oh no! Oh my gosh!

221
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,220
It's her.

222
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:42,400
What do you want with me, or perhaps more accurately with Chrollo?

223
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:44,060
I have a question.

224
00:13:44,060 --> 00:13:46,700
What are you doing in the game?

225
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:49,680
Well, what to do now?

226
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:52,980
Well, if I talk, I know how they'll react.

227
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:58,040
They'll do everything in their power to keep the spiders from the Nen Exorcist.

228
00:13:58,040 --> 00:14:06,440
That could be interesting in and of itself, but I don't want to delay my fight with Chrollo any longer than I have to.

229
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:09,200
I came here to look for Chrollo.

230
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:16,040
He's still crippled by Kurapika's Nen, but there's actually a way to remove it.

231
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:17,500
Exorcism.

232
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:18,560
You knew?

233
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:21,740
Well, that will make this much easier.

234
00:14:22,180 --> 00:14:26,680
I'm looking for Chrollo to pass that along, but I have no leads.

235
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:33,080
Before long, I remembered that some of the spiders were interested in this game.

236
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:39,700
So, of course, if I can locate them, they might be able to tell me where Chrollo is.

237
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:44,760
And using his handle, all but guarantees they'll try to contact me.

238
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:49,200
Okay. So he was just pretending to be a member of the Phantom Troop.

239
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:49,980
Yeah.

240
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:53,120
Now, I have a question for you.

241
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:57,960
Tell me, did the two of you really come all the way out here just to ask me that?

242
00:14:58,440 --> 00:14:59,520
Yeah, sure did.

243
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:02,520
Um...

244
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:08,420
The truth is, we're here looking for people who are really strong.

245
00:15:08,940 --> 00:15:11,180
And we were hoping you might join us.

246
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:15,220
Huh? All right.

247
00:15:15,780 --> 00:15:18,040
May I ask why you're looking for strong people?

248
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:21,740
Hey, wait a minute. I don't think I like this. It's risky.

249
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:24,840
It sure is. You don't know who this guy is, risky.

250
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:27,100
What? Of course I know who he is.

251
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:32,360
Not personally, but I feel a certain kinship with him.

252
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:38,940
The city of love, Ai-Ai, isn't very far from here.

253
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:44,760
You can meet all kinds of people. You might even find the strength that you're looking for.

254
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:53,220
What exactly did you mean about him lying?

255
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:57,380
Well, technically, I should have said that he wasn't telling the truth.

256
00:15:57,380 --> 00:15:58,720
But how could you tell?

257
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:00,860
It was really more of a hunch.

258
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:01,500
Seriously?

259
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:05,660
After lying for 50 years myself, I can recognize a fellow liar.

260
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:09,480
That's actually pretty convincing.

261
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:15,980
It's obvious he's hiding something, so best to keep him around until we can find out what.

262
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:18,780
Plus, he's really strong, isn't he?

263
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:20,000
Yeah.

